# ESP32-C5 only. ESP-IDF loads this after sdkconfig.defaults (and before any
# board overlay) whenever the target is esp32c5, so other chips keep the
# shared 16 KiB, internal-RAM TCP configuration.
#
# lwIP pbufs and TCP segments, and the Wi-Fi driver's heap allocations, prefer
# the 8 MB PSRAM, so TCP windows stop costing scarce internal RAM: on the C5
# DevKitC-1 this left 11 KiB more internal RAM free at idle and 12-32 KiB more
# under load. That pays for 32 KiB windows in each direction, which double the
# per-flow ceiling (~5.2 Mbit/s at 50 ms RTT, from ~2.6). Wi-Fi DMA buffers
# stay in internal RAM. Measured with tools/coexist/bench, including a soak
# with BLE active (tools/coexist/README.md).
#
# 64 KiB windows were faster still on the bench but drove free DMA-capable RAM
# to ~1 KiB under bulk TX, so they need fewer Wi-Fi TX buffers first.
# If PSRAM fails to initialize (CONFIG_SPIRAM_IGNORE_NOTFOUND), lwIP falls
# back to internal RAM and the larger windows cost it there.
CONFIG_SPIRAM_TRY_ALLOCATE_WIFI_LWIP=y
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_SND_BUF_DEFAULT=32768
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_WND_DEFAULT=32768
